The legal texts come from ZambiaLII (Southern African Institute for Policy and Research, on the Laws.Africa Peachjam platform):

  ZambiaLII, https://zambialii.org, point-in-time versions of each act, read from archived copies of its
  pages on the Internet Archive (https://web.archive.org), retrieved 2026-10-28.

Licence and terms, as ZambiaLII states them: CC BY-NC 4.0, crediting ZambiaLII as the source (https://zambialii.org/terms-of-use/).
CC BY-NC 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/legalcode

Attribution:

  Source: ZambiaLII (https://zambialii.org), licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0).

The texts may be used only for non-commercial purposes. This repository is private; whether and how it
may be published is the owner's decision under these terms.

Changes made by Lexifina: each version was converted to one Markdown file per provision, one paragraph per
line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; editorial notes, Part and Chapter headings were left out;
and the versions were arranged as git commits credited to the laws ZambiaLII names for each change.
The wording of the law was not changed. Neither ZambiaLII nor Laws.Africa endorses this repository.

Further sources (added 2026-11-27):

  Ministry of Justice, Republic of Zambia, https://www.moj.gov.zm (Acts as passed; read from the Internet
  Archive's captures where the Ministry's own files no longer load). No terms stated.

  Judiciary of Zambia, https://judiciaryzambia.com (court Acts and rules). No terms stated.

  FAOLEX, Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, https://www.fao.org/faolex/ (secondary
  copies). Terms: reuse for non-commercial purposes with credit. Source: FAOLEX (FAO).

  WIPO Lex, World Intellectual Property Organization, https://www.wipo.int/wipolex/ (secondary copies).
  Terms: https://www.wipo.int/tools/en/disclaim.html

Zambian legislation is a Government work under the Copyright and Performance Rights Act (s. 12(2)); it is
reproduced here unaltered, without charge, with its source named in each commit.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the
tools) are dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Further sources (2026-11-27 (second pass)):

  Ministries and regulators of Zambia publishing Acts and statutory instruments on their own sites: Securities
  and Exchange Commission, Department of Immigration, Bank of Zambia, Energy Regulation Board, Zambia Revenue
  Authority, Anti-Corruption Commission, Electoral Commission, Human Rights Commission, National Prosecution
  Authority, Zambia Environmental Management Agency, Road Transport and Safety Agency, Competition and Consumer
  Protection Commission, Zambia Public Procurement Authority and others (named in each commit). No terms stated.

  Southern African Development Community, https://www.sadc.int (Treaty, protocols, amending agreements,
  charters). No terms stated.

  Common Market for Eastern and Southern Africa, https://www.comesa.int (Official Gazette of COMESA). No terms
  stated.

  Judiciary of Zambia decisions whose download link no longer loads: read from the Internet Archive's captures
  (https://web.archive.org) of the Judiciary's own files (private case-law repository only).
